  "editorial": [
    "The one-beat pickup is followed by 31 common bars. From page 5 system 2 the route moves directly to Last on system 3. First and second endings, the repeat and the D.S. are skipped for a single chorus.",
    "The chorus begins in C major and the Last ending restores the three-flat signature. Pitches carry the printed accidentals, including the natural B in the final approach.",
    "The lower printed vocal line is used where the final system offers an upper ad lib. The optional upper ad lib is outside this guide.",
    "The fixed 100 BPM rehearsal uses measured note lengths at fermatas. Small grace notes take one tick each from the following written attack. Piano sixteenth triplets use four ticks each.",
    "The two printed bass rolls use simultaneous attacks. The rehearsal uses fixed velocities and nominal durations for marked accents and staccatos.",
    "The piano has separate upper and lower counterline tracks for independent note lengths. The export contains no lyrics or archive images."
  ],
